From 27a53d404f3533f566b7cafe951844b02043d686 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 22:50:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/12] fix(frontend): sync chat messages by clientMessageId
 and full server history
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

syncSessionMessages computed the append set positionally
(messages.slice(serverCount)): if another device had appended a message in
the meantime, the wrong tail was re-sent and the two copies diverged
silently. The diff is now keyed on clientMessageId (unique per session in
the database); rows written before the field existed still match by
position. The trailing-assistant patch only fires when the local and server
rows are the same message.

The server list itself was one 200-row page, so older messages of a long
chat always looked "missing". fetchAllSessionMessagesFromServer walks
`before` pages (capped at 5000 rows, then the sync is refused rather than
guessed). The full-history PUT used for prompt deletion now always builds
its payload from that complete list via `reconcile`, instead of pushing the
locally loaded 50-message window on the first attempt — which replaced the
whole history with the visible part.

mergeRemoteChatSessions had three branches producing the identical object,
so local always won regardless of updatedAt. It now takes the newer copy's
fields (title keeps its own rule, Agent selection stays server-owned) and
pickMergedMessages prefers the newer list over the longer one, so a
deletion made elsewhere reaches this device.

